5</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00006454-200007000-00003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Knott</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Street</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bailey</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Cameron</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Febrile adults presenting to the emergency department: outcomes and markers of serious illness</article-title><source>Emerg Med J</source><year>2004</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>170</fpage><lpage>174</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14988341</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/emj.2002.001933</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van Laar</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A prospective study of fever in the accident and emergency department</article-title><source>Clin Microbiol Infect</source><year>2003</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>878</fpage><lpage>880</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14616713</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1469-0691.2003.00665.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>YL</given-names></name><name><surname>Tseng</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsay</surname><given-names>PK</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Chiu</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Procalcitonin as a marker of bacterial inf